PHASE 7 — THE ON-CHAIN TRANSACTION (IMPRESSIVE MOMENT)
============================================================

Create scripts/verify_chain.py. This is the only phase that broadcasts real
transactions. It is a manual script, not a jac test.

7.1 — Preconditions
  Assert .env has POR_TOKEN_ADDRESS, POR_ATTESTATION_ADDRESS, SEPOLIA_RPC_URL,
  DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY. If any is missing, exit with a clear message.

7.2 — Read pre-state
  Connect via web3. Read:
    - Deployer's PoRToken balance.
    - Total supply of PoRToken.
    - The next PoRAttestation token id (query _nextId via a read — if the field
      is private, infer from the last AttestationMinted event).
  Print all three.

7.3 — Run the happy path against a fresh asset
  Reset the store. Seed the asset. Run DemoControl(path="happy"). Query
  GetAsset. Extract the Cover stamp's justified_amount.
  Print: "Cover justified amount: <value>".

7.4 — Mint via Act
  POST /walker/Act/{node_id} with body {requested_amount: 1_000_000,
  recipient: deployer_address, token_address: ..., attestation_address: ...}.
  Capture the response. Assert:
    - minted == true.
    - amount == min(1_000_000, justified).
    - tx is a 0x-prefixed 32-byte hex string.
    - nft_id > 0.

7.5 — Verify the on-chain effects
  Wait for the tx to confirm (web3.eth.wait_for_transaction_receipt).
  Read post-state:
    - Deployer's PoRToken balance increased by exactly the minted amount.
    - Total supply increased by exactly the minted amount.
    - The Minted event was emitted with the correct amount and the JSON reason
      string.
    - The PoRAttestation token with the reported id exists, is owned by the
      recipient, and its record struct matches: mintedAmount, coverageUsed,
      priceTime, reserveTime, stampSummary.
  Print all values.

7.6 — Explorer links
  Print:
    - https://sepolia.etherscan.io/tx/{tx_hash}
    - https://sepolia.etherscan.io/token/{token_address}
    - https://sepolia.etherscan.io/token/{attestation_address}?a={nft_id}
  Manually open each link and confirm they resolve to the correct tx and NFT.

7.7 — Refusal paths do not broadcast
  Run yellow path. Spawn Act. Assert no tx hash is returned and no new
  Minted event appears on-chain (compare block number before and after).
  Run unknown path. Same assertion.

7.8 — Summary print
  Print a final block:
    MINTED: <amount> pUSD
    JUSTIFIED: <justified>
    REQUESTED: 1_000_000
    SIZED BECAUSE: min(requested, justified) = <amount>
    TX: <hash>
    NFT: <id>
    EXPLORER: <link>
  This is the "impressive transaction out" confirmation.

